.TH MV7WEB 1 "August 28, 2026" "shure-mv7 0.1.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mv7web \- unofficial Linux control for a Shure MV7+ microphone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mv7web
.RB [ \-addr
.IR address ]
.RB [ \-open ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mv7web
opens the Shure MV7+ vendor HID interface and serves an embedded web console.
The console controls gain, DSP, monitoring, reverb, mute, and LED settings.
This independent project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by
Shure Incorporated.
.PP
The default address is
.BR 127.0.0.1:8090 .
The server provides no authentication or TLS and should normally remain bound
to the loopback interface.
.PP
Remote control is supported, for example when the microphone is connected to
a Linux streamer PC. Prefer an SSH tunnel to the default loopback listener. A
non-loopback listen address may be used on a trusted private network when host
firewall rules restrict access. Never expose the server directly to the
internet.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-addr " address"
Set the HTTP listen address. The default is 127.0.0.1:8090.
.TP
.B \-open
Stop an older mv7web process owned by the current user, then open the console
in the default browser with xdg-open. This ensures desktop launches use the
currently installed binary after an upgrade.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/62-shure-mv7plus.rules
Grants the active desktop user access to the Shure MV7+ hidraw interface.
.SH HARDWARE
Shure MV7+ USB devices with vendor ID 14ed and product ID 1019 are supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg-open (1),
.BR udev (7)